From 7f88e657495b73f47fe1a6ea776a8b5cf412558f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:05:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] arm64: configs: Add rhodep_defconfig

The configuration for the moto g82 5G as a k3s node, derived from
negroni_defconfig, which runs on negroni (OnePlus 10 Pro): negroni's configuration
resolved on this tree, then changed and saved again with savedefconfig,
so symbols that negroni gets through selects are explicit here.

Changes from negroni:
- SM6375 in place of SM8450: its pin and clock controllers, SMD RPM
  (clocks, regulators, power domains over GLINK), MPM, the OSM L3
  interconnect, the QMP UFS PHY (built in, the root filesystem is on
  UFS), the USB HS PHY, SDHCI, ath10k SNOC and the PAS remoteprocs.
- The GENI serial engines (UART, I2C, SPI), as on negroni: the charger, the
  Type-C logic and the fuel gauge are on GENI I2C buses.
- SMEM, SMP2P and GLINK over SMEM set explicitly: on negroni the pmic_glink
  drivers select them.
- negroni's display (DRM_MSM and its panel) and pmic_glink stack
  (battery manager, UCSI, Type-C muxes) left out; there is no DSI panel
  driver for this phone and the charger is discrete.
- UFS inline crypto off: the ICE block is described but not used.
- The APSS watchdog built in and the hung task detector on, as on negroni's
  v7.3-rc5 branch.
- Kernel BTF (full DWARF instead of reduced), which Cilium's BPF
  masquerade needs.
- The null TTY driver built in. Motorola's bootloader rewrites every
  console= on the command line, ours included, to console=null; with
  NULL_TTY that is the ttynull console, without it there is no console
  at all, /dev/console cannot be opened and initramfs-tools' final
  exec of run-init, which redirects to it, kills PID 1.
- CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-rhodep": phone kernels are named by device codename.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
